{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39659808",
      "title": "Prefer Computed Values & Avoid Unnecessary State Management",
      "sourceHash": "0aaf3c665de555915dc104320d1e35e95a9b26eb2a64368a219850d6eb69dafa",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.93,
          "end": 3.48,
          "en": "Therefore, in the GameBoard component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 8.48,
          "en": "we can get rid of this activePlayerSymbol prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.15,
          "end": 13.02,
          "en": "and we'll use the onSelectSquare prop here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.02,
          "end": 16.173,
          "en": "as a value for the onClick prop on the button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 21,
          "end": 25.44,
          "en": "So we're no longer going to manage our game state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 25.44,
          "end": 26.61,
          "en": "in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 26.61,
          "end": 29.04,
          "en": "Instead, we're going to lift it up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 29.04,
          "end": 32.76,
          "en": "Therefore, of course, we'll need to fix this gameBoard here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.76,
          "end": 35.43,
          "en": "which we're trying to map into a grid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.43,
          "end": 37.44,
          "en": "But we'll do this in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.44,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "For the moment, I'll leave this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "as it is and get rid of this useState import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 45.363,
          "en": "and switch back to the App component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.35,
          "end": 51.35,
          "en": "Here it's still handleSelectSquare that's executed with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 51.96,
          "end": 55.14,
          "en": "of the onSelectSquare prop, which we're still passing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.14,
          "end": 59.463,
          "en": "to GameBoard when a button is clicked in that gameBoard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 61.83,
          "end": 64.89,
          "en": "So that's still happens, but now here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 64.89,
          "end": 69.423,
          "en": "in handleSelectSquare, we wanna update our turns,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 70.35,
          "end": 72.48,
          "en": "using this functional approach here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 72.48,
          "end": 75.24,
          "en": "because the new turns array will depend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 75.24,
          "end": 77.133,
          "en": "on the old turns array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.15,
          "end": 81.45,
          "en": "And in here, I simply wanna add a new entry",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 81.45,
          "end": 85.56,
          "en": "to this array of turns that we took in this game.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 85.56,
          "end": 88.89,
          "en": "For this, we can create an updatedTurns constant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 88.89,
          "end": 92.46000000000001,
          "en": "where we copy the existing turns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 92.46000000000001,
          "end": 94.2,
          "en": "because we should update this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 94.2,
          "end": 96.213,
          "en": "in an immutable way as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.14,
          "end": 100.14,
          "en": "And now I wanna insert the new turn.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.14,
          "end": 103.74000000000001,
          "en": "So the information about which player clicked which button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.74000000000001,
          "end": 107.58,
          "en": "in front of the old turns so that the first item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.58,
          "end": 111.18,
          "en": "in this array is always the latest turn.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.18,
          "end": 114.63,
          "en": "For this here, we can add a new thing in this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 114.63,
          "end": 118.53,
          "en": "And now the only question is how should the information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.53,
          "end": 122.19,
          "en": "about a single turn in our game look like?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.19,
          "end": 124.02,
          "en": "And of course, there will be different ways",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 125.55,
          "en": "of implementing this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 125.55,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "but I'd say it makes sense to store an object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 134.4,
          "en": "so that our gameTurns state will eventually be an array full",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 134.4,
          "end": 138.93,
          "en": "of objects and we want to know which player clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 138.93,
          "end": 142.53,
          "en": "on which square and the square can be identified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 142.53,
          "end": 145.05,
          "en": "by row and column index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 148.26,
          "en": "So therefore here in handleSelectSquare,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 148.26,
          "end": 152.19,
          "en": "I need to know which row and which column was clicked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.19,
          "end": 157.19,
          "en": "or which rowIndex and column index was selected in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 157.71,
          "end": 160.38,
          "en": "So that here in this object which we're adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 160.38,
          "end": 164.67000000000002,
          "en": "to this updatedTurns array, we can describe our square",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 164.67000000000002,
          "end": 169.2,
          "en": "with a nested object maybe where we set row equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 169.2,
          "end": 174.2,
          "en": "to rowIndex and col equal to colIndex like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 175.35,
          "end": 178.953,
          "en": "So that's the new object we're adding to this turns array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 181.59,
          "en": "Now, of course, we also need to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 181.59,
          "end": 184.21,
          "en": "which player clicked that square",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 185.1,
          "end": 187.8,
          "en": "and therefore, we can add a player property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 187.8,
          "end": 190.14,
          "en": "to this turn object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 190.14,
          "end": 194.58,
          "en": "And here we can use activePlayer to store the symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 194.58,
          "end": 196.683,
          "en": "of the player that's currently active.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 197.55,
          "end": 200.55,
          "en": "Though doing that is not optimal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 200.55,
          "end": 203.52,
          "en": "because when using activePlayer here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 203.52,
          "end": 207.39,
          "en": "we're technically merging two different states",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 207.39,
          "end": 210.06,
          "en": "and we're using this function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 210.06,
          "end": 212.67000000000002,
          "en": "for updating the gameTurns state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 212.67000000000002,
          "end": 215.85,
          "en": "for the reasons I mentioned earlier to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 215.85,
          "end": 218.94,
          "en": "that when the schedule state update is performed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 218.94,
          "end": 222.42000000000002,
          "en": "we are definitely working with the latest state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 222.42000000000002,
          "end": 224.04,
          "en": "but we don't have that guarantee",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 224.04,
          "end": 227.67000000000002,
          "en": "for activePlayer because that's from a different state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 227.67000000000002,
          "end": 230.57999999999998,
          "en": "Therefore, a better way of deriving the symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 230.57999999999998,
          "end": 235.05,
          "en": "of the currently activePlayer is to add a new variable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 235.05,
          "end": 237.45,
          "en": "in this function that we're passing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 237.45,
          "end": 239.79,
          "en": "to the state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 239.79,
          "end": 242.64,
          "en": "that could be named currentPlayer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 242.64,
          "end": 245.643,
          "en": "and by default, that's maybe X let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.63,
          "end": 248.43,
          "en": "But I then wanna add a if statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.43,
          "end": 251.55,
          "en": "and check if in our previous turns array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 251.55,
          "end": 253.59,
          "en": "if the first element in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 253.59,
          "end": 256.65,
          "en": "which will always be the latest turn as you know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 256.65,
          "end": 261.21,
          "en": "if there the player is equal to X.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 261.21,
          "end": 265.95,
          "en": "So if the latest stored turn in our existing turns state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 265.95,
          "end": 270.95,
          "en": "if that turn was performed by the player with the symbol X.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 274.8,
          "en": "And if that's the case, I instead wanna set currentPlayer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.8,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "to O because we then know that now it was the player",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 281.7,
          "en": "with the symbol O that performed this turn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 281.7,
          "end": 285.27,
          "en": "because the latest turn before that was performed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 285.27,
          "end": 287.613,
          "en": "by the player with the symbol X.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 289.59000000000003,
          "end": 293.7,
          "en": "Now, of course, there might be no latest turn stored.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 293.7,
          "end": 297.65999999999997,
          "en": "For example, initially it's an empty array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 297.65999999999997,
          "end": 301.44,
          "en": "and therefore, we can add another condition here and check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 301.44,
          "end": 306.44,
          "en": "if previous Turns.length is greater than zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 307.92,
          "end": 311.793,
          "en": "And then the latest turn was by this player.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 312.99,
          "end": 316.23,
          "en": "This way we only take a look at this latest turn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 316.23,
          "end": 319.05,
          "en": "if we have at least one turn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 319.05,
          "end": 322.23,
          "en": "and now we can use this currentPlayer information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 322.23,
          "end": 324,
          "en": "which in the end is derived",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 324,
          "end": 328.83,
          "en": "from our turns state to set the symbol of the player",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 328.83,
          "end": 331.62,
          "en": "who was responsible for this turn.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 331.62,
          "end": 333.48,
          "en": "And now with all that done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 333.48,
          "end": 336.42,
          "en": "we finally got this updated array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 336.42,
          "end": 339.45,
          "en": "and we can return updatedTurns here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 339.45,
          "end": 343.56,
          "en": "as a new value for the gameTurns state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 343.56,
          "end": 344.61,
          "en": "because that's in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 344.61,
          "end": 348.27,
          "en": "what this state updating function here is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 348.27,
          "end": 351.36,
          "en": "And it is a rather long state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 351.36,
          "end": 353.76,
          "en": "But this is absolutely something you'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 353.76,
          "end": 357.6,
          "en": "in React projects and it is a state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 357.6,
          "end": 361.47,
          "en": "that makes sure that we update state in an immutable way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 361.47,
          "end": 364.92,
          "en": "and that we're not merging different states.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 364.92,
          "end": 367.83,
          "en": "And with that, we're now one step closer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 367.83,
          "end": 371.7,
          "en": "to using this gameTurns state for both the log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 371.7,
          "end": 375.423,
          "en": "and the GameBoard, which are the things we'll work on next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}